[agent] ## Summary
[agent] Feature table **`scores6bd170`** version 1 is live in the feature store with:
[agent] - **Record key:** `account_id` (primary key)
[agent] - **Columns:** exactly `account_id` (string), `score` (double)
[agent] - **Rows:** 80 — one per account
[agent] - **Online enabled:** `online_enabled: true` → available for low-latency real-time lookup, in addition to the offline store
[agent] ### How the work ran (all platform-side)
[agent] 1. **Ingest** — Loaded `data/feature_history.csv` (559 revisions, 80 accounts) into an offline feature group `feature_history_raw` v1 via `hops fg insert`.
[agent] 2. **Point-in-time scoring (on Trino, server-side)** — A single `hops sql` query did the as-of-T selection and scoring:
[agent]    - Window `row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY account_id ORDER BY event_time DESC)` filtered to `event_time <= 1773223200000`, keeping only `rn = 1` → the most recent revision **at or before T** per account; later revisions excluded.
[agent]    - `score = round(1/(1+exp(-(0.741·f1 + 0.3204·f2 − 0.099·f3 + 0.3323))), 6)` using the model weights/bias.
[agent]    - All 80 accounts had a valid revision ≤ T.
[agent] 3. **Write** — Inserted the 80 result rows into the online+offline FG `scores6bd170` v1.
[agent] ### Verification
[agent] - Spot-checked A0000: as-of revision (event_time 1772802240000) → z ≈ 1.0546 → sigmoid ≈ **0.741666**, matching the stored value.
[agent] - `hops fg info` confirms schema, `online_enabled: true`, PK `account_id`.
[agent] - `hops fg preview` reads the data back through the platform's own read path (HQS).
[agent] Note: a couple of CLI calls needed `--no-verify`/correct catalog discovery — the offline table is a **Delta Lake** table under schema `<project>_featurestore` (catalog `delta`), and the Trino endpoint serves an IP-mismatched cert so `--no-verify` was required. The `score` displayed as `0.9145939999999999` in preview is just the IEEE-double rendering of the value that was rounded to 6 decimals (0.914594) before insert.
